# Every path records its owner, and since 20 October 2026 this map is a merge
# control: the code-owner-review ruleset (.github/rulesets/code-owner-review.json)
# requires an approving review from a code owner on every pull request into
# development, staging and main. GitHub requests that review automatically on any
# pull request the owner did not open — Dependabot's included — which is why
# dependabot.yml carries no `reviewers` key (GitHub removed it in favour of this file).
#
# One developer today means every line resolves to the same person, and GitHub
# never lets an author approve their own pull request. The owner's own pull
# requests — every one opened under the owner's account, by hand or by an agent —
# therefore merge through the logged administrator bypass, and that deliberate
# merge is the owner's approval. See docs/implementation/03-github-workflow.md §3 and §6.

